# Tasks Backlog

This file tracks follow-up work that is not active right now. Use `PLANS.md` for active, blocked, or recently completed execution.

When work starts, promote or link the item into `PLANS.md` before implementation. Keep detailed execution checklists out of the backlog.
After promoted work closes, remove the backlog item by default once useful information lives in `PLANS.md`, canonical docs, an archive note, or an external tracker.
Mark backlog items `done` only when the record remains useful. Archive only when future-useful rationale, external tracker mapping, repeated deferral history, or explicit retention requirements justify it.
After context compaction, interruption, resume, or milestone closure, reconcile backlog status with `PLANS.md` before code changes.

## Backlog Item: <title>

Status: planned | parked | blocked | promoted | done
Priority: low | medium | high

### Activation Trigger
- Condition that makes this work worth starting.

### Goal
One paragraph describing the intended end state.

### Next Safe Action
1. First bounded step.

### Exit Criteria
- Clear done conditions.

### Promotion Notes
- If promoted, link or name the matching `PLANS.md` active plan.

### Cleanup Notes
- Remove this item if it has no activation trigger, no next safe action, or only repeats completed work.
- If closed, choose one: remove by default; mark `done` only for a useful audit trail; archive under `docs/archive/backlog/YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>.md` only for future-useful rationale or explicit retention.
- Do not leave stale next safe action or milestone status text in a `done` item unless it links to explicit follow-up work.
